---
number: 566
title: O Prince of Peace
author: J. T. Graves
composer: J. Harker
sp_category: "37"
topic: The Second Coming of Jesus
---

[verse 1]
O Prince of Peace, who once didst rise
In splendid triumph to the skies,
Before the rapt disciples’ eyes,
O come, Lord Jesus, quickly come!
For Thy appearance all things pray,
All nature sighs at Thy delay,
Thy people cry, “No longer stay,”
O come, Lord Jesus, quickly come!

[verse 2]
Hear, Thou, the whole creation’s groan,
The war-swept nations’ plaintive moan,
The lands made deserts all forlorn;
O come, Lord Jesus, quickly come!
See signals of distress unfurled
By states on stormy billows hurled;
Thou Polestar of a shipwrecked world,
O come, Lord Jesus, quickly come!

[verse 3]
By doubts and sorrows inly pressed,
By foes beleaguered and oppressed,
Hear the strong cry of world unrest!
O come, Lord Jesus, quickly come!
Hope of the tried and faithful host,
Their only glory, joy and boast,
Without Thy advent all is lost
O come, Lord Jesus, quickly come!

[verse 4]
Come with Thy beauteous diadem;
Come with embattled cherubim,
Come with the shout of seraphim.
O come, Lord Jesus, quickly come!
Come on Thy seat of radiant cloud;
Come with the Archangel’s trumpet loud;
Come, Saviour, let the heavens be bowed
O come, Lord Jesus, quickly come!
